Sensitive parameters in CHEASE:

NSMOOTH: control whether the plasma boundary can be well contructed by 
         Fourier expansion.  =0 is good.

SOLPDA: very important to control the q-profile, =0.5 is better than
        =0.4

B0EXP, R0EXP: should be set up in the NAMELIST in order to get correct 
              current in the output.

NCSCAL=4: no value of q at one point is needed to be specified,
          important for constructing equilibrium from EQDSK

Boundary shape (R,Z): should be normalized such that R0=1
 
psi>0:  consider the sign of P' and TT'

When change COMMON blocks, don't forget to change block size in COMDIM

Good parameter set for CHEASE:
   NS=NT=60, NCHI=256, MSMAX=60, shape is good, q is bad at center
   NS=NT=46, NCHI=92,  MSMAX=22, both shape and q are good
     
Very important!: always choose NCHI as even number

In order to better resolve magnetic axis, use the following packing for 
the sigma-mesh:
   NMESHC=1, NPOIDC=1, SOLPDC=0.8, CPLACE=0.0,CWIDTH=0.020,

Opt-in frozen-restart wall replacement:

NINWALL=1 is supported only with NOPT=1, NSURF=6 and NSYM=0. It reads
normal EXPEQ geometry (NDATA=2) after loading NIN. The EXPEQ plasma
vertices must match the frozen native plasma point set within 1e-12 in
the frozen native coordinate frame. The runtime mesh-axis RZ0 is not an
input origin and is not subtracted. No translation, scale or phase is
fitted. The EXPEQ preamble and profile block do not alter native state.
Only intermediate/outer walls and their native angular splines are rebuilt;
the NIN file, plasma splines, equilibrium coefficients and profiles remain
unchanged. Default NINWALL=0 retains the existing restart behavior.

This permits NVEXP=8 to pin a supplied physical intermediate wall on an
integer vacuum surface while refining NV without solving the equilibrium
again. It does not qualify individual coil endpoints or field convergence.
Always verify the actual OUTRMAR/OUTVMAR geometry and preserve source hashes.
